    "fixture": "Commodore PET 2001 (1977) cold power-on screen (\"*** COMMODORE BASIC *** / 7167 BYTES FREE / READY.\") in VICE xpet -model 2001, double-size on an 800x600 X root; golden INTERNAL snapshot restores the untouched cold boot, and nothing is typed before the bake or after the restore. Keyboard proven 2026-08-09 AFTER the bake, against the restored fixture and at the tile's shipped 80/80 pacing: the four-line demo program typed and LISTed correctly (lit phosphor 1841 → 6077), then RUN plotted into screen RAM (→ 10285), then loadvm golden returned the frame to the baked 1841. Keyboard-only exhibit (no mouse); AC97 audio (silent — the 1977 machine had no sound hardware)."
